{
  "description": "Hybrid logical clock vectors (ARCHITECTURE §5.1, ADR 0009). Hand-written. Text form: 13 decimal digits of wall ms, '-', 4 lowercase hex digits of counter, '-', 8 lowercase hex digits of node id. Lexicographic order of the text = clock order. now(phys): wall = max(phys, last.wall); counter = last.counter + 1 if wall == last.wall else 0; if counter > 0xffff then wall += 1, counter = 0; if wall is outside 0..9999999999999 (MAX_WALL) fail with wall_out_of_range; last = result (own node). receive(h) at physical time phys (after an import, with the file's max_hlc): if h.wall > phys + 86400000 (MAX_DRIFT_MS, 24 h) fail with clock_ahead; else last = max(last, h) by text order; the next now() then sorts after h. A failed step leaves last unchanged (expect_last). An empty last means no clock yet. Every step carries phys, the physical clock in ms at that step.",
